# Benchmark instance data.
#
# Downloaded from Netlib and MIPLIB and fully reproducible with
# benchmarks/fetch_netlib.py and benchmarks/fetch_miplib.py, which verify every
# file against the SHA-256 recorded in the committed manifests. About 5 MB of
# regenerable input does not belong in the history; the manifests, the frozen
# selections and the provenance notes -- which are what make a result row
# traceable -- are committed.
benchmarks/instances/*/raw/
benchmarks/instances/*/mps/
benchmarks/instances/*/tools/
benchmarks/instances/netlib/netlib_readme.txt
__pycache__/
*.pyc
